{
  "A start and an end date in one field: typed through two masks, or picked on two months side by side, from ready-made ranges, within the dates and the span allowed. The value is a `[start, end]` pair.": "",
  "Presets": "",
  "`presets` puts ready-made ranges beside the calendars: `true` for the kit’s, or your own, each made when it is chosen. `calendars={1}` shows one month.": "",
  "`min`, `max` and `disabledDates` bound both ends, typed or picked; `minDays` and `maxDays` bound the span, and the calendars offer only the days within while the end is being picked. A failed rule says which.": "",
  "With a time, and in another locale": "",
  "Each side is a masked input in the locale’s order (`22.11.2006`); a whole, real date is taken as it is finished, an emptied side becomes `null`. Tab moves from the start to the end.": "",
  "On the popup the first pick is the start, the second the end: an earlier second pick becomes the start. With both chosen, the next pick starts a new range. While the end is being picked, the pointer shows the range it would make.": "",
  "The calendars show the start’s month and the next; paging one pages the other with it.": "",
  "A list beside the calendars; a press takes the range and closes.": "",
  "Alt+Down opens the popup; in it the calendars take the arrow keys, Enter picks; Escape closes, and clears the field when `clearButton` is on and the popup is closed.": "",
  "Two text boxes named “<label>, Start date” and “<label>, End date” in the kit language; the field’s label marks the start.": "",
  "A dialog named “Choose date”; the calendars are the kit’s grids, the presets a list box.": "",
  "The rules speak in the kit language; a rule of your own in yours.": "",
  "The field. `data-type`.": "",
  "The inputs and the glyph between them.": "",
  "The popup, each calendar, the presets.": "",
  "Units: the glyph between the inputs (`icon`, `bg`), the list of presets (`focus`, `beside`).": "",
  "Place: a calendar on the popup.": "",
  "Between the calendars and the presets.": "",
  "The calendar’s cells in a range: its ends and the days between, drawn by each language.": "",
  "The `[start, end]` pair; either `null` while not chosen. `x-model` binds it two-way.": "",
  "With `datetime` the time is typed after the date; the calendars keep it.": "",
  "The dates allowed, on both ends, typed or picked.": "",
  "The least and the most days a range may span, the end counted from the start; while the end is picked the calendars offer only days within.": "",
  "`true`: the kit’s ready-made ranges beside the calendars (today, yesterday, the last 7 and 30 days, this and last month); your own as `{ text, range: () => DateRange }`.": "",
  "Months side by side on the popup; two stay a month apart as one is paged.": "",
  "The popup closes once both ends are picked.": "",
  "As on the `DateBox`.": "",
  "Shown in an empty box.": "",
  "The clear button; the button that opens the calendars.": "",
  "The ends as properties of their own.": "",
  "The start’s and the end’s inputs.": "",
  "The popup with the calendars; `onOpened`, `onClosed`.": "",
  "Empties both ends.": "",
  "As on every field: an unfinished date, a date outside `min`, `max` or `disabledDates`, a start after the end, a span under `minDays` or over `maxDays`.": "",
